This is the `unsafe-mode` branch of the Venastine Research Harness.

It carries two settings that `main` does not have, and that no npm release
ever will:

    config.UNSAFE_NO_APPROVAL   no tool call is ever asked about
    config.UNSAFE_NO_SANDBOX    shell commands run on the HOST, Docker or not

Both ship False. The branch is a capability, not a posture -- checking it
out changes nothing until you set one.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
--------------------
`scripts/prepublish-check.mjs` refuses to publish any tree containing it.
That check lives on `main`, so it arrives here by merge and cannot be lost
by a bad conflict resolution -- and it also catches the reverse accident,
this branch's code merged INTO main and published from there. A published
npm version can never be replaced, only deprecated, so that direction is
the unrecoverable one.

DO NOT DELETE THIS FILE, and do not merge this branch into `main`.

WHO THIS IS FOR
---------------
Security researchers who want an unbounded harness for testing and who
accept the consequences. Any vulnerability that requires one of these
settings is a DOCUMENTED RISK, not a finding -- see SECURITY.md.

The relevant reading is ROADMAP_v2.md section 90 (UM1-UM8) for what the
switches do and why they are shaped this way, and section 40 (UN1-UN6) on
`main` for why the posture cannot be changed mid-session.

KEEPING UP TO DATE
------------------
    git fetch origin && git merge origin/main

The delta is deliberately small so that stays cheap.
